# "staging run did not finish" markers written next to a staged EP tree
# (pack-ep.mjs / resolve-pro.mjs). A stale one must survive `git status` so a
# failed build cannot be mistaken for a clean one.
#
# Note on redundancy — measured, not assumed (`git check-ignore -v <file>`):
# for the marker the EP pipeline actually writes, which lands INSIDE
# src-tauri/resources/builtin-ep/, rule 69 (the directory rule) matches too and
# is the one git reports. The reason is NOT "the last matching rule wins": in a
# scratch repo `dir/` on line 1 beats `*.incomplete` on line 2, and swapping
# those two lines only moves which line number reports the directory rule — it
# still wins. A matching directory rule excludes the subtree by itself: git
# never descends into an excluded directory, so no other pattern is consulted
# for the paths beneath it. (Control, same scratch repo: with a NON-matching
# `dir/other/` on line 1, `*.incomplete` on line 2 does win — so ordering does
# decide among the patterns actually evaluated for a given path.)
# This line is NOT redundant in general: a root level `foo.incomplete` is matched
# by this rule and by nothing else, and --stage-dir is unvalidated, so it may
# point anywhere in the tree. Kept for that reason; do not read "rule 69 already
# covers it" as licence to delete this.
*.incomplete

# Built-in locale codegen (written by generate-builtin-locales.mjs; not committed)
src/locales/builtinLocales.ts

# Generated capabilities (merged from default_host.json + plugin capabilities by resolve-drivers.mjs)
